    "site_desc": "This site is located on a Delta peat island in a cornfield that is flooded during the non-growing season (beginning in October or November and ending in early February). Peat is roughly 2 meters thick in this area and soil organic matter  ranges from 10 to 30%. Three soil types dominate this site:  Ryde Clay Loam, Peltier Mucky Clay Loam, and Rindge Muck.  Crop management was consistent for 25 years prior to and during the measurement period. The field was fertilized twice and irrigated twice during the growing season.",
